:5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:36:06-07:00","id":987064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/986345-question-about-effective-wyrd#post986345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Effective Wyrd. It's a neat way to make characters who excel in one area without necessarily being that potent to a casual &quot;power level&quot; scan.<br /> <br /> My question is, can it exceed 10? Forever and a Day says no, but Potent Kith notably does not specify. I can see it being a reasonable cap (after all, you can trade those dots under Sanctity of Merits if your Wyrd gets high enough to make them irrelevant) but I can also see the argument that if somebody wants to invest in reaching Effective Wyrd 15 why stop them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can technically go higher. However, this would affect things like dice pools, kith advantages, and the like. But it wouldn't affect things like Glamour capacity and expenditure, or trait limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Da